      "questionEn": "How do you tell one friend or familiar person not to do something?",
      "answerEn": "Put no before the verb's special negative-command form. If the verb uses te, put te between no and the verb.",
      "noteEn": "For a regular -ar verb, the negative form usually ends in -es: hablar becomes no hables. Regular -er and -ir verbs usually end in -as: comer becomes no comas. A short word such as te goes before this negative form, as in no te levantes.",
